cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UniMRI: A Unified Python Framework for MRI Raw Data Processing and Reconstruction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Istiyak Amin
    family-names: Santo
    alias: istiyakamin
repository-code: "https://github.com/istiyakamin/UniMRI"
url: "https://github.com/istiyakamin/UniMRI"
abstract: >-
  UniMRI is an open-source Python framework that provides a common data model and
  computational abstraction layer for MRI raw data acquired from different
  scanners, vendors, and acquisition strategies (Cartesian and non-Cartesian),
  enabling reconstruction algorithms to operate independently of the original
  vendor format.
keywords:
  - MRI
  - image reconstruction
  - k-space
  - ISMRMRD
  - non-Cartesian
  - NUFFT
license: MIT
version: 0.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
